<h2>Planning for Repeated Use</h2>
<p>For a trade show model, the requirements extend beyond its appearance at the first event. Packing, handling, setup and storage all influence how practical the model will be for future presentations.</p>
<p>The Aviation Garage project brought those considerations into model development. Testing sectional configurations helped establish where the model should separate and where it should remain continuous.</p>
<p>The result was a construction strategy that balanced architectural presentation with the practical demands of a traveling display.</p>
